    <h2 id="move-in-checklist-h">Move-in checklist</h2>
    <p><strong>Tenant Next Steps Prior to Move In</strong></p>
    <p>Use this checklist to keep track of the items needed before receiving keys to your new home.</p>

    <h3>1. Complete Lease Agreement</h3>
    <p>Sign and return all lease documents, addendums, and any required forms.</p>

    <h3>2. Set Up Utilities</h3>
    <p>Transfer all utilities into your name and provide proof before move-in.</p>

    <h3>3. Gather Move-In Funds</h3>
    <p>Be prepared to bring the following to get keys:</p>
    <ul class="plain-list">
      <li>Remaining security deposit</li>
      <li>First month’s rent</li>
      <li>Landlord-billed utilities (such as sewer and trash)</li>
      <li>If you do not have a housing voucher and your credit score is below 550, a double deposit of two months’ rent is required, along with the remaining security deposit.</li>
      <li>Tenants receiving Section 8 assistance will only be responsible for their portion of the first month’s rent and landlord-billed utilities.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4. Obtain Occupancy Permit (if applicable)</h3>
    <p>If required by the local municipality, obtain your occupancy permit and provide a copy.</p>

    <h3>5. Move In / Get Keys</h3>
    <p>On or about the lease start date, meet with the property manager for a walkthrough and to obtain keys once all the above items are completed.</p>

    <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="{{ '/assets/docs/bfp-move-in-checklist.pdf' | url }}" download>Download the move-in checklist (PDF)</a></p>
